confirm-turn-interruption-with-escape

Lane: frontend

FlatPatch: confirm-turn-interruption-with-escape

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Require explicit confirmation before Esc cancels an active turn while preserving native pending-steer submission and other key behavior.

Requires: none

Provides: Show an input-area confirmation with Keep working selected by default; preserve drafts, image preparation and goals until Stop turn is accepted, and dismiss or reject confirmations after the original turn changes or ends.

Boundary: Own only frontend confirmation at actual Esc cancellation routes, including blocking and asynchronous questions. Keep pending-steer interrupt-and-submit unconfirmed, and preserve native interruption, other interrupt bindings, local Esc navigation, task execution and backend protocols.

Verification: Focused ChatWidget, owned-transcript, question, image, goal and lifecycle tests verify deferred cancellation, stale choices, inline placement and preserved drafts; native pending-steer, Vim and mention tests verify immediate interrupt-and-submit without confirmation.


